    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-23T09:20:37+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T09:20:37+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T22:50:37Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-22T22:50:37Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure lies near the NT border. A slow moving high pressure system in the Tasman Sea maintains a ridge across eastern parts of the state. A trough of low pressure over the far west is forecast to slowly move eastwards on Friday. Another trough and multiple cold fronts move over the state over the weekend. A ridge of high pressure moves into the west on Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW014" description="North East Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-23T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-22T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far northeast in the late morning and afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far northeast in the afternoon. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light in the middle of the day then becoming southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures in the low to mid 30s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. Slight chance of a shower in the evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening, possibly severe with damaging winds and large hail south of Yunta in the late afternoon and evening. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending north to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the early morning then tending north to northwesterly in the middle of the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Leigh Creek, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding in the far northeast. Winds southeast to southwesterly 30 to 45 km/h becoming southwesterly 35 to 50 km/h during the day then tending southerly 30 to 45 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 20 to 28.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
